{:org/id :org-deu-schuetzenvereine
 :org/name "Schützenvereine and shooting fraternities (Schützenbruderschaft, Swiss Schützengesellschaft, Nordic skytterlag)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-fraternal-order
 :org/category :cat-fraternal
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :regional
 :org/region-primary :region-europe
 :org/countries ["DE" "CH" "AT" "NO" "DK" "FI" "BE" "NL" "IT"]
 :org/founding-date 1400
 :org/founding-note "Town shooting brotherhoods predate the sport federations by centuries; many trace to late-medieval militia and church guild charters."
 :org/instance-count-estimate 13502
 :org/member-count 1357240
 :org/member-count-basis "source-pinned for Germany's sport federation only: the Deutscher Schützenbund reported 1,357,240 members in 13,502 organisational units as of 31 December 2025 — a FOURTH consecutive year of growth (+7,482 members, of which 4,104 were under 21) while the number of clubs FELL by 99. Swiss, Austrian and Nordic bodies are separate and not included, and the historical Schützenbruderschaften that sit outside or alongside the sport federation are not counted here at all."
 :org/proxy-metric "sport-federation membership"
 :org/proxy-bias "Counts the sport aspect of a body that is often also a processional and church-linked brotherhood. A village Bruderschaft that crowns a Schützenkönig, walks in the parish procession and shoots twice a year appears in this figure only as a sports club, or not at all."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/registration-note "German clubs are e.V.; the older brotherhoods often hold property and endowments predating that form and registered late."
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "Town and village societies built around a shooting range and an annual festival that crowns a king — simultaneously a sport club, a drinking society, a uniformed processional body and, in Catholic regions, a parish institution."
 :org/coverage-note "Recorded because members rising while clubs fall is a pattern the corpus otherwise only saw in decline stories: the federation is growing and its local bodies are still closing, and a membership figure alone hides that."
 :org/related-org "org-global-hunting-fishing-associations"
 :org/source-name "Deutscher Schützenbund, Bestandserhebung (dsb.de)"
 :org/source-url "https://www.dsb.de/jugend/news/artikel/news/der-deutsche-schuetzenbund-waechst-im-vierten-jahr-in-folge"
 :org/source-date "2025-12-31"
 :org/source-tier :primary
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-26"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

{:org/id :org-global-prison-inside-communities
 :org/name "Communities inside prison (inmate councils, faith congregations, inside AA/NA groups, lifers' and study groups)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-peer-support
 :org/category :cat-mutual-aid
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-europe
 :org/countries ["NO" "SE" "DK" "US" "GB" "BR" "JP" "ZA" "IN"]
 :org/founding-date 1900
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown — prison populations are counted precisely and the associations inside them are not counted at all. Chaplaincy and programme statistics record attendances at sessions, which is neither membership nor continuity, since transfer and release end participation without ending the group."
 :org/proxy-metric "programme and chaplaincy attendance"
 :org/proxy-bias "Attendance at a permitted session, recorded by the institution that permits it. A group that meets on the wing without permission is by construction absent from the figure, and the count rises when the authority opens more sessions rather than when the community grows."
 :org/legal-registration :mixed
 :org/registration-note "The Nordic inmate councils are statutory bodies with a right to be consulted and no legal personality; nearly everything else inside exists only by permission of the custodial authority, which can withdraw it without giving a reason. This is a distinct cause of non-registration from the five already recorded — not informality, criminalisation, persecution, ineligibility or copyright, but association held at another party's discretion."
 :org/governance-model :mixed
 :org/mission-statement "Associations formed by people who cannot leave and did not choose their neighbours — councils that negotiate conditions, congregations, recovery meetings, study and lifers' groups — carrying literacy, sobriety and dispute-settlement work that the institution does not do."
 :org/coverage-note "Being listed as a member can itself be the hazard here, as with the underground schools: affiliation recorded inside a prison can be read as gang classification and affect release. The corpus records the form and does not seek rolls."
 :org/related-org "org-global-reentry-prisoner-families"
 :org/data-provenance "llm-recall-unverified"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

{:org/id :org-global-textile-circles
 :org/name "Quilting bees, knitting circles and stitching collectives (arpilleristas, mola cooperatives, sewing groups)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-recurring-salon
 :org/category :cat-hobby-interest
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-north-america
 :org/countries ["US" "CL" "PA" "GB" "JP" "IN" "ZA" "PE" "BD"]
 :org/founding-date 1800
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown and structurally invisible: circles meet in homes, church halls and back rooms, and the ones that do get counted are counted as customers of a yarn shop or as suppliers to a craft cooperative. The Chilean arpillera workshops of the 1970s-80s were counted, when at all, by the church body that smuggled the work out."
 :org/legal-registration :mostly-unregistered
 :org/registration-note "Export-oriented craft cooperatives (molas in Guna Yala, embroidery collectives in South Asia) register in order to sell; the domestic circle that produced the same skill does not and never did."
 :org/governance-model :consensus
 :org/mission-statement "Groups of mostly women who bring handwork to a shared table — the object under construction is the pretext, the talk is the point, and the circle doubles as a savings club, news exchange and care rota."
 :org/coverage-note "Recorded with the political case stated: Chilean arpilleristas stitched scenes of disappearance under the dictatorship and the panels left the country as craft, which made a sewing circle a documentation network. A form this easy to dismiss as a pastime has repeatedly been the only association a repressive state left open to women."
 :org/related-org "org-global-recurring-salons"
 :org/data-provenance "llm-recall-unverified"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

{:org/id :org-global-motorcycle-clubs
 :org/name "Motorcycle clubs and riding communities (MCs, riding clubs, HOG chapters, bōsōzoku)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-hobby-society
 :org/category :cat-hobby-interest
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-north-america
 :org/countries ["US" "DE" "AU" "JP" "BR" "ZA" "GB" "NZ"]
 :org/founding-date 1947
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown across the form — manufacturer-run owner groups publish chapter counts and claim memberships in the high hundreds of thousands, patch-holding MCs publish nothing by design, and independent riding clubs are uncounted. The three are routinely conflated in press figures."
 :org/legal-registration :mixed
 :org/registration-note "Three registration regimes in one form: manufacturer owner groups are company programmes, riding clubs register as ordinary associations, and outlaw MCs are proscribed outright in several jurisdictions — so the same activity is a marketing scheme, a club and a criminal association depending on which body is doing it."
 :org/governance-model :hierarchical
 :org/mission-statement "Groups organised around riding together, with a patch or a chapter charter marking membership — a form whose internal hierarchy (prospect, member, officer) is unusually explicit, and whose commercial version is owned by the manufacturer of the machine."
 :org/coverage-note "The manufacturer-owned owner group belongs with the agency-owned fan club and the platform-hosted creator community: in all three the community's roll, name and continuity are the property of a company that also sells to it."
 :org/related-org "org-global-creator-membership-communities"
 :org/data-provenance "llm-recall-unverified"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

{:org/id :org-global-road-communities
 :org/name "Road communities (long-haul truckers, CB radio channels, truck-stop regulars, driver networks)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-status-based-community
 :org/category :cat-labor-coop
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-north-america
 :org/countries ["US" "IN" "BR" "TR" "ZA" "AU" "RU" "MX"]
 :org/founding-date 1970
 :org/founding-note "CB radio channel 19 became the North American drivers' open channel in the 1970s; the Indian dhaba and Turkish lokanta stop are older and serve the same function."
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown — driver counts exist as an occupational statistic and say nothing about the community, which forms on a radio channel, at a stop, or in a WhatsApp group and has no roll. Trade unions and owner-operator associations count only the organized minority."
 :org/proxy-metric "licensed driver headcount"
 :org/proxy-bias "An occupational census, not a community measure: it counts everyone who holds the licence, including drivers who never enter the social world of the road, and misses the non-drivers (stop owners, mechanics, sex workers, dispatchers) who are part of it."
 :org/legal-registration :unregistered
 :org/governance-model :consensus
 :org/mission-statement "A community of people who are structurally alone and moving — traffic and hazard information, breakdown help, meals and sleep at the same stops, and a channel that is open to anyone in range — held together by shared condition rather than shared place."
 :org/coverage-note "Recorded because the corpus is otherwise organised around places and rolls, and this form has neither: the membership test is being on the road tonight."
 :org/related-org "org-global-gig-collectives"
 :org/data-provenance "llm-recall-unverified"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}
]
